{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 127, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without a direct input-to-output skip, a strong conv on the node2->output edge supplies much-needed capacity and gradient flow, while with a skip present it adds little (exps 7, 8 and 10 vs 1-5)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node1 does not feed the output directly, the residual input->output path matters more (exp 19 vs 11 and 18)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual where none existed helps more than swapping out an existing conv or pool for a skip (exps 11 and 17 vs 12 and 14)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Pruning the node1->output edge is more harmful when there is no input->output skip to compensate (exps 32 and 33 vs 31 and 35)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with parameter-free pooling loses capacity, unlike replacing none or skip (exp 51 vs 52-54)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the residual skip on the input->output edge typically hurts trainability more than deleting a conv there (exps 62 and 64-67)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a pooling op on the final edge with an identity removes harmful smoothing, giving larger gains than replacing a conv (exp 88 vs 82 and 83)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a 1x1 conv on a missing node1->output edge adds capacity, whereas replacing a skip or 3x3 conv with it is neutral or harmful (exps 71 and 75-78 vs 72 and 79)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "A conv on edge 1->2 is wasted when node1 receives no input because edge 0 is none (exp 41 vs 44)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Turning the final conv into a skip removes key capacity when there is no other direct route to the output (exp 81 vs 82 and 85)."}], "tok": 17326, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3